WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.560
Speaker 1: We appear to be approaching potentially&nbsp;
two more arrests of failed former President Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:15.540
Trump. First and foremost is that Fannie&nbsp;
Willis in Georgia is stepping up security and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:22.260
precautions for this next season, so to speak, of&nbsp;
announcing indictments that will start in July and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:27.600
run through September. There is the belief that&nbsp;
Trump is getting indicted there. But separately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:35.040
there is a Rolling Stone article. Trump's lawyers&nbsp;
warn him, get ready to be indicted by the feds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.140
The former president has angrily complained&nbsp;
in response to predictions that if the Justice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:47.280
Department is going to charge him, then what&nbsp;
about Joe Biden? What about Joe Biden? And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.200
article says Some of Trump's lawyers and advisers&nbsp;
have given the former president an unwelcome,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:59.280
if not unexpected message in recent weeks. You&nbsp;
should expect to get indicted this year. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:07.020
we've talked before about the seemingly un derail&nbsp;
the bill train that is Trump speeding towards the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:13.200
Republican nomination. And in those hypotheticals,&nbsp;
the question about what could derail it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:21.660
has mostly gone to if Trump gets arrested and is&nbsp;
so bogged down by criminal cases that he quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:26.580
literally can't get out on the campaign trail&nbsp;
in any substantive way, it starts to affect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.660
the Republican electorate and people who currently&nbsp;
say they would be voting for Trump in the primary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:37.500
were it today. Move on to someone else, maybe&nbsp;
DeSantis or maybe someone else. But short of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.320
Trump seems to have an unobstructed path to the&nbsp;
nomination. And yet we now seem to be potentially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:50.040
within months of Trump getting arrested two&nbsp;
more times. The article also says several legal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:54.060
and political counselors to Trump have bluntly&nbsp;
informed him they expect the Justice Department&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:59.220
to charge him in the criminal investigation&nbsp;
into his hording of highly classified documents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.480
following the end of his presidency. Two sources&nbsp;
familiar with the matter tell Rolling Stone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:09.480
This, of course, comes on the heels of Trump's&nbsp;
indictment by local prosecutors in Manhattan in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:14.640
April for falsifying business records. Later this&nbsp;
summer, officials in Fulton County, Georgia, are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.980
expected to make a decision about whether or not&nbsp;
to indict Trump. Trump's attorneys and confidants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.660
told Trump that though they view the federal&nbsp;
investigation as B.S., they would be surprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:29.460
at this point if he wasn't charged, particularly&nbsp;
for alleged obstruction of justice, and have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:34.500
urged Trump to prepare for yet another historic&nbsp;
fight. Looks like they're going for it. One of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.060
sources says people close to the former president&nbsp;
have discussed with him what we think is going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:45.720
happen soon and how he and everyone else needs&nbsp;
to be ready for it. It would be crazy not to. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.760
there's two things going on here. One, there are&nbsp;
very real political implications. We are quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:56.820
getting into the heat of a very hotly contested&nbsp;
Republican primary. It will be an unprecedented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:02.640
situation where the current president will be&nbsp;
running for reelection. That's Joe Biden against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:09.600
a former president. Who was already defeated by&nbsp;
Biden and then will be running again against him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:15.360
Unprecedented. And you throw into the middle of&nbsp;
that already one, maybe two, maybe a third arrest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.700
and it is going to be complete and total chaos&nbsp;
if we go beyond the political implications.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:27.480
Progress is slow, but we are seeing some progress.&nbsp;
Now, I still don't believe that we are going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:33.600
to see Trump do a day of prison or jail. I don't&nbsp;
think we're going to see it in any of these cases.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:41.700
However, if you look at the degree to which&nbsp;
this has gone from, this stuff should be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:48.120
investigated to there are investigations&nbsp;
to we're talking to a grand jury to. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.140
looking like the grand jury wants to convict.&nbsp;
Trump has been arrested once and maybe and may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.140 --> 00:04:01.920
end up arrested three times. That is major&nbsp;
progress in seeking to find justice for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:08.040
alleged wrongs of the Trump presidency. So we&nbsp;
will be following the forthcoming possibility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:15.240
of more arrests very closely. It is important to&nbsp;
also understand that while Trump seems to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:20.700
an unobstructed path to the nomination, unless&nbsp;
multiple arrests take him off the campaign trail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:26.880
the so called anti-Trump Republican movement&nbsp;
seems to be imploding. Let's talk about that next.

